{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J4 0a94 CLOSED. Change 1011 patch set 2: LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, 0 unresolved, submittable=True — the macos-py3.13 job that failed on patch set 1 now passes, confirming the test-helper root cause was the real one and not a coincidence.\n'UNBLOCKED: none' on close is CORRECT, not a bug: J6 9fd4 needs BOTH J4 and J5 c97f closed, and J5 is still open.\nBOARD: J1 closed, J2 closed, J4 closed, J3 in_progress (implementation validated, awaiting the full suite before commit), J5 open (plan already PASSED, independent), J6/J7/J8 blocked.\nJ5 FEASIBILITY CHECKED EARLY rather than discovered at claim time: J5 needs a real Dockerized Jira (pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1 on localhost:2990). Verified docker 29.2.1 with a RUNNING daemon on this host, so J5 is genuinely verifiable here rather than authorable-but-unprovable. Started pulling the pinned image in the background so it is warm when J5 starts — the image is large and the pull would otherwise be dead time.\nNote on J5's shape: every test in tests/live_jira_dc/ carries the EXISTING 'integration' marker, so 'make test' (-m 'not integration and not external') excludes it by construction with no Makefile filter change. Its teardown oracle deliberately avoids post-deletion SEARCH-INDEX assertions (ADR 0037 §3 forbids them — Jira's index lags both creates and deletes) and instead polls each issue's direct REST endpoint until 404, which is index-independent."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785354224478283001,"uuid":"cccf2f35-2221-4d0d-9acb-a266a9d38aa8"}